w21-info-friction
-----------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data or
weights.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Dimitris Panagopoulos, Adolfo Perrusquía, Yang Xing and Weisi Guo.
"Model-Free Runtime Measurement of Task-Relevant Information".
arXiv:2611.14111, v1, submitted 10 Nov 2026. Primary category cs.RO,
cross-listed cs.AI. Acquisition-State Telemetry (AST) is the method's name
in the abstract, not the title.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.14111
Licence: arXiv non-exclusive distribution licence,
http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/ (a paper licence, not a
software grant).

Code: the abs page Comments field says "Code available", but the abs page
gives no link. The code is UNVERIFIED and unlocated; none was found or
used.

Method only: the idea of two signals over information gathering, progress
across unresolved requirements and friction when recurrent evidence brings
no gain. The fail-closed stop when friction passes a declared bound, and
the expiry rule, are this sketch's own rules, not the paper's. No text,
figures, tables or data from the paper are copied into the code; the PDF
was not read; no domain or reinforcement learning experiment was re-run.
The paper's claims appear only in paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked
UNVERIFIED.
